nterface (vtnet2) into service as a new OPNsense zone (\\\"optb\\\"/LANB, 172.31.98.1/24) via config.xml + configctl reconfigure, added a firewall pass rule for the zone, and gave node3's matching interface (enp8s0) a persistent static address (172.31.98.2/24) via its existing NetworkManager profile. Verified node3 reaches node1 on lan-b and reaches node2 (10.100.55.11, lan-a) with the traffic actually routed/forwarded through node1 (confirmed via forced host route + TTL decrement + tcpdump on both of node1's interfaces). Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes with boot-identity proof and post-restart recovery verification, including confirming the new OPNsense zone and firewall rule persisted across node1's reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed node1 (OPNsense), node2, node3 interfaces to identify the unconfigured lan-b link (node1 vtnet2 <-> node3 enp8s0) versus the pre-existing lan-a segment (node1 vtnet0 <-> node2/node3 enp1s0), by temporarily assigning test addresses and pinging between candidate interfaces\",\"Edited /conf/config.xml on node1 to add interface 'optb' (if vtnet2, descr LANB, static 172.31.98.1/24) and a filter pass rule for the optb network; applied with configctl interface reconfigure optb and configctl filter reload\",\"Configured node3's pre-existing 'Wired connection 2' NetworkManager profile for enp8s0 with static 172.31.98.2/24 and gateway 172.31.98.1, activated it persistently\",\"Verified node3 -> node1 (172.31.98.1) and node3 -> node2 (10.100.55.11) reachability, and proved the node2 path is actually routed through node1 via a forced /32 route, TTL decrement, and tcpdump captures on node1's vtnet2 and vtnet0 interfaces\",\"Captured pre-restart baselines (boot_id / kern.boottime, addresses, connectivity) on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node2 via systemctl reboot, polled until exec returned, confirmed changed boot_id and recovered connectivity to node1\",\"Restarted node3 via systemctl reboot, polled until exec returned, confirmed changed boot_id, confirmed the static lan-b address persisted via NetworkManager, and re-verified connectivity to node1 and node2\",\"Restarted node1 via /sbin/reboot, polled until exec/SSH returned, confirmed changed kern.boottime, confirmed the optb zone/IP and its firewall pass rule survived reboot (re-applied from config.xml), and re-verified node3's connectivity to both node1 and node2\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Identify which of node1's unconfigured interfaces faces lan-b and connects to node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8e352d1b9b7646cc\",\"cmd-fc4e26d23b8d4931\",\"cmd-dce3f97ad4db4681\",\"cmd-c3bfb8cd21ba426e\",\"cmd-5b95423eb2f643e3\",\"cmd-e2ffaa9b0827443c\",\"cmd-296f376a482b4686\"],\"summary\":\"ifconfig/ip addr surveys plus ping tests isolated vtnet1 as unconnected and vtnet2<->node3 enp8s0 as the live lan-b link\"},{\"requirement\":\"Bring node1's lan-b interface into service as its own zone with an address\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0dff4c634c064f75\",\"cmd-8748e7fe0fbc4261\",\"cmd-c0a7f28fe0e147d9\",\"cmd-7d24b8450c3d4fb1\"],\"summary\":\"config.xml edited to add optb interface (vtnet2, 172.31.98.1/24) and a pass rule; configctl interface reconfigure optb + filter reload applied it; ifconfig and pfctl -s rules confirm the zone and rule are live\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 reaches node1 on lan-b\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-db0140422bb24a5f\",\"cmd-4549030444f547b5\"],\"summary\":\"node3's enp8s0 given persistent static 172.31.98.2/24 via NetworkManager; ping from node3 to 172.31.98.1 succeeds\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 reaches node2 on lan-a through node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-db0140422bb24a5f\",\"cmd-67301369c79b4e8f\",\"cmd-e441d823eae24df5\"],\"summary\":\"Forced node3 to route 10.100.55.11 via node1's lan-b IP; ping succeeded with ttl=63 (one hop through node1); tcpdump on node1 showed the ICMP traffic ingress on vtnet2 and egress on vtnet0, proving cross-zone forwarding\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory resta